# clagentic-lite repo-level semgrep --exclude-rule ladder (docs/GATES.md
# Gate 4c "SAST").
#
# Format: one semgrep rule id per line; # comments and blank lines are
# stripped. Each active rule id becomes an --exclude-rule <id> flag on both
# the baseline-commit and full-tree semgrep invocations (see
# _sast_exclude_rule_flags, scripts/gates.sh).
#
# No exclusions are currently active for this repo. A prior version of this
# file listed python.sqlalchemy.security.sqlalchemy-execute-raw-query with a
# justification tying it to injection-safe sqlalchemy/psycopg2/
# sql.Identifier usage; BOBBIE's PR #159 security review found no such
# usage anywhere in this codebase, and the engram IDs cited alongside it did
# not resolve in LORE. Shipping a permanent SAST exclusion whose stated
# rationale does not correspond to any code in the repo is worse than
# shipping no exclusion -- it is an unexplained hole in the gate for every
# downstream user -- so the entry was removed rather than kept unverified.
# A future exclusion added here must cite a concrete, verifiable finding in
# THIS repo's own code.
